rule ctc_child_amount_base with provenance "26 USC 24(a)":
the ctc child amount base is 1000 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D.

rule ctc_phaseout_reduction_per_increment with provenance "26 USC 24(b)(1)":
the ctc phaseout reduction per increment is 50 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D.

rule ctc_phaseout_increment with provenance "26 USC 24(b)(1)":
the ctc phaseout increment is 1000 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D.

rule ctc_joint_threshold_base with provenance "26 USC 24(b)(2)(A)":
the ctc joint threshold base is 110000 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D.

rule ctc_unmarried_threshold_base with provenance "26 USC 24(b)(2)(B)":
the ctc unmarried threshold base is 75000 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D.

rule ctc_separate_threshold_base with provenance "26 USC 24(b)(2)(C)":
the ctc separate threshold base is 55000 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D.

rule ctc_child_age_ceiling_exclusive with provenance "26 USC 24(c)(1)":
the ctc child age ceiling exclusive is 17 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D.

rule ctc_full_taxable_year_months with provenance "26 USC 24(f)":
the ctc full taxable year months is 12 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D.

rule ctc_fraud_disallowance_years with provenance "26 USC 24(g)(1)(B)(i)":
the ctc fraud disallowance years is 10 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D.

rule ctc_reckless_disallowance_years with provenance "26 USC 24(g)(1)(B)(ii)":
the ctc reckless disallowance years is 2 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D.

rule ctc_modified_adjusted_gross_income with provenance "26 USC 24(b)(1)":
the ctc modified adjusted gross income of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the adjusted gross income of the tax unit is an amount M
    and the ctc foreign earned income exclusion adjustment of the tax unit is an amount K
    and the ctc possession income exclusion adjustment of the tax unit is an amount P
    and the ctc puerto rico income exclusion adjustment of the tax unit is an amount Q
    and N = M + K + P + Q.

rule ctc_qualifying_child with provenance "26 USC 24(c)":
a person is ctc qualifying child if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the ctc child of the person satisfies dependency rules
    and the age of the person is a number N
    and the ctc child age ceiling exclusive is a number M
    and N < M
    and the person is ctc child deduction allowed
    and it is not the case that the certain noncitizen exception of the person applies.

rule ctc_child_identification_requirement_satisfied with provenance "26 USC 24(e)(1)":
a person is ctc child identification requirement satisfied if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the person is qualifying child name included on return
    and the person is qualifying child tin included on return
    and the person is qualifying child tin issued on or before return due date.

rule ctc_qualifying_children_count with provenance "26 USC 24(a), (c), (e)(1)":
the ctc qualifying children count of a tax unit is a number N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the tax unit is a tax_unit
    and a number M is the count of each P such that
        a person P is a ctc qualifying child of the tax unit
    and a number Q is the count of each K such that
        a person K is a ctc qualifying child of the tax unit
        and it is not the case that K is ctc qualifying child
    and a number S is the count of each R such that
        a person R is a ctc qualifying child of the tax unit
    and a number U is the count of each T such that
        a person T is a ctc qualifying child of the tax unit
        and it is not the case that T is ctc child missing identification
    and N = M - Q - (S - U).

rule ctc_taxpayer_identification_requirement_satisfied with provenance "26 USC 24(e)(2)":
a tax unit is ctc taxpayer identification requirement satisfied if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the tax unit is a tax_unit
    and it is not the case that the tax unit is taxpayer identification number issued after return due date.

rule ctc_full_taxable_year_requirement_satisfied_1 with provenance "26 USC 24(f)":
a tax unit is ctc full taxable year requirement satisfied if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the taxable year months of the tax unit is a number N
    and the ctc full taxable year months is a number M
    and N >= M.

rule ctc_full_taxable_year_requirement_satisfied_2 with provenance "26 USC 24(f)":
a tax unit is ctc full taxable year requirement satisfied if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the tax unit is taxable year closed by reason of taxpayer death.

rule ctc_prior_claim_restriction_satisfied with provenance "26 USC 24(g)":
a tax unit is ctc prior claim restriction satisfied if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the tax unit is a tax_unit
    and it is not the case that the ctc fraud disallowance period of the tax unit applies
    and it is not the case that the ctc reckless or intentional disregard disallowance period of the tax unit applies
    and it is not the case that the tax unit is prior deficiency denial without required eligibility information.

rule ctc_phaseout_threshold_base with provenance "26 USC 24(b)(2)":
the ctc phaseout threshold base of a tax unit is an amount if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the ctc phaseout joint threshold of the tax unit applies
        and the ctc joint threshold base is the amount
        otherwise the ctc phaseout separate threshold of the tax unit applies
        and the ctc separate threshold base is the amount
        otherwise the tax unit is a tax_unit
        and the ctc unmarried threshold base is the amount.

rule ctc_phaseout_threshold with provenance "26 USC 24(b)(2), 24(h)(3)":
the ctc phaseout threshold of a tax unit is an amount if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the tax unit is ctc subsection h special rules apply
        and the ctc phase out threshold under subsection h of the tax unit is the amount
        otherwise the ctc phaseout threshold base of the tax unit is the amount.

rule ctc_maximum_before_phaseout with provenance "26 USC 24(a), 24(h)(2), 24(h)(4)":
the ctc maximum before phaseout of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the tax unit is ctc subsection h special rules apply
        and the ctc maximum before phase out under subsection h of the tax unit is N
        otherwise the ctc qualifying children count of the tax unit is a number M
        and the ctc child amount base is an amount K
        and N = M * K.

rule ctc_phaseout_amount with provenance "26 USC 24(b)(1)":
the ctc phaseout amount of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the ctc phaseout reduction per increment is an amount M
    and the ctc modified adjusted gross income of the tax unit is an amount K
    and the ctc phaseout threshold of the tax unit is an amount P
    and the ctc phaseout increment is an amount Q
    and a number R = K - P
    and the maximum of 0 and R is a number S
    and N = M * ceiling(S / Q).

rule ctc_before_advance_payments with provenance "26 USC 24(a), 24(b), 24(e), 24(f), 24(g), 24(h)":
the ctc before advance payments of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the tax unit is ctc taxpayer identification requirement satisfied
        and the tax unit is ctc full taxable year requirement satisfied
        and the tax unit is ctc prior claim restriction satisfied
        and the ctc maximum before phaseout of the tax unit is an amount M
        and the ctc phaseout amount of the tax unit is an amount K
        and a number P = M - K
        and the maximum of 0 and P is N
        otherwise the tax unit is a tax_unit
        and N = 0.

rule ctc_after_advance_payments with provenance "26 USC 24(j)(1)":
the ctc after advance payments of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the ctc before advance payments of the tax unit is an amount M
    and the ctc advance payments received of the tax unit is an amount K
    and a number P = M - K
    and the maximum of 0 and P is N.

